## Constraints

- Author the motion with keyframes and easing/Bezier curves. Do not write a
  physics simulation loop (no per-frame velocity/gravity integration in
  JavaScript). The animation must be fully described by the keyframes and
  their easing, exactly as {{ framework }} normally expresses motion.
- Animate the ball's POSITION only. Do not keyframe scale, rotation,
  opacity or any other property -- the bounce must read entirely from the
  position curves.
- The starting source files are already in this directory. Edit them
  directly; do not restructure the project layout.
{%- if framework == "css" %}
- Edit `style.css`. Use a `@keyframes` rule on `#ball`, driven by its
  `transform` (`translateX`/`translateY`) and `animation-timing-function`.
{%- elif framework == "gsap" %}
- Edit `animation.js`. Use GSAP (`gsap.to` / `gsap.timeline`) to animate
  `#ball`'s position (`x` / `y`). GSAP is already loaded globally
  via the `<script>` tag in `index.html` -- do not replace it with a bundled
  import.
{%- elif framework == "lottie" %}
- Edit `animation.json` directly (standard Lottie/Bodymovin format). The
  ball is the shape layer named `ball`; animate its position (`ks.p`)
  with keyframed values and bezier easing (`i`/`o`).
  `index.html` already loads it with lottie-web; do not change the player
  setup.
{%- endif %}
- When you believe the animation is complete and matches the scene above,
  call `finish`.

